  "details": "Any light grip on the opposite hand that opened the Quick Menu will unintentionally scroll any UI element after doing an open hand Gesture on the Valve Index.\nHow to reproduce:\n- On Open Beta, with Valve Index controllers on both hands\n- Make sure the Valve Index palm strap is not strapped too tight\n- Make a closed fist with the Left hand and keep it in a closed fist position\n- Open the Quick Menu on the Right Hand (by pressing the Quick Menu button on the Right Hand)\n- Open any of the following menus of your choice:\n--- Quick menu on the Right hand > Volume > point the cursor onto a slider with the Left hand\n--- Quick menu on the Right hand > Select user > point the cursor onto the quick menu with the Left hand\n--- Quick menu on the Right hand > Worlds (which opens the System Menu) > Point the menu on any row that is scrollable with the Left hand\n- As long as the Left hand is doing a fist, the menu works by pressing the left trigger on left hand as expected\n- Now, make a full open hand gesture with the Left hand by opening all fingers\n- From now on, any light grip on the Left hand will cause scrolling elements to grab\n- There is no force required to activate the grab with the light grip, just lightly closing the Left thumb and the middle finger around the controller should be enough to trigger the grip\nObserved:\n- The volume sliders of the Quick menu will move\n- The Quick menu will scroll up and down\n- The worlds row of the System menu will scroll laterally\nExpected:\n- Light grip should not cause an interaction with any scrollable element in the menu\nAdditional comments:\n- Opening the Quick Menu on the Left hand will cause the light grip to occur on the Right hand",
